    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **governance.test.js** - Missing named export\n**Problem**: The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't being exported from `src/finetune/index.js`.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports for the constants imported from schema.js:\n```javascript\nexport { APPROVAL_STATUSES, DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS, GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS, RISK_LEVELS };\n```\nThis maintains backward compatibility with the default export while adding the named exports the tests expect.\n\n### 2. **eval/index.test.js** - Incorrect toxicity metric signature\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was being called with `(outputs, references)` from `runEvaluations`, but its signature was `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. This caused the references array to be misinterpreted as banned terms, resulting in false toxicity flags.\n\n**Fix**: Updated the function signature to properly accept the references parameter:\n```javascript\nexport function toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)\n```\nAlso made it more robust by converting bannedTerms to an array with `toArray()`.\n\n## Results\n\u2705 All 28 frai-core tests passing (8 test files)\n\u2705 All public exports preserved for backward compatibility\n\u2705 No test files modified - only source code fixed",
